+\section{Robustness analyses}
+
+These analyses replay stored predictions and measured cost tables; no model was retrained and no device was re-measured. They are robustness checks and do not replace the primary results.
+
+\paragraph{Per training seed and sequence-grouped split} Table~\ref{tab:robust} repeats the main comparisons for each training run separately and for a fit/held-out split by whole recording (ACDC) or city sequence (Cityscapes) instead of alternating index; calibrators, risk-target grid, T-hard thresholds, and operating points are refitted on the new fit half only. Night and fog contain only two and three recordings, so their sequence split places different recordings in the two halves. Every conclusion holds in every seed and under the sequence split; the sign of D $-$ T-hard changes across seeds, consistent with no detectable difference.
+
